    pr_ref:  # 93a4
    description: "FOUND while landing INV-potuf, as its non-vacuity check: with typescript's\nsinks finally deriving, the end-to-end flow STILL was not found -- and the\njavascript control returned the same clean verdict, which is what identified\nthis as pre-existing and language-general rather than anything INV-potuf did.\n\nTHE DEFECT. `emit_module_attribute_refs` takes a `caller_symbol` used as the\nedge `src`. Its own docstring says the root argument may be \"the file root for\nmodule-level reads, or a function body for per-function emission\" -- so the\nhelper supports both. EVERY tree-sitter caller passes the FILE pseudo-symbol\nand the file root:\n\n    js_ts.py:5979   file_mod_sym         go.py:3186    file_pseudo_symbol\n    java.py:2604    (file symbol)        cpp.py:1689   (file symbol)\n    rust.py:2580    (file symbol)\n\nPython is the exception: its own in-module helper (WI-guhok) anchors to the\nenclosing callable, which is why the identical flow shape IS caught in python.\n\nMEASURED, with the control that separates the two source kinds. Same claim\n({source_taint: host_secret, prohibited_sink_zone: host_fs}), same sink\n(`fs.writeFileSync`), same enclosing function, only the SOURCE KIND differs:\n\n    call-kind source       os.hostname()          -> rc 1 violated    (found)\n    attribute-kind source  process.env.API_KEY    -> rc 0 confirmed   (MISSED)\n\nThe edges show exactly why:\n\n    calls            src=...:3-6:dump:function   dst=...:fs:0-0:writeFileSync:unresolved\n    module_attr_ref  src=...:1-1:file:file       dst=...:process:0-0:process.env:attribute\n\nThe source and the sink do not share a caller, so no flow can be constructed.\nIdentical in javascript and typescript.\n\nSCALE, from the derived catalogue rather than estimated: javascript has 50\ntaint sources of which **21 are kind=attribute** -- including the whole\n`process.env` / `process.argv` family, which is the canonical way a Node\nprogram reads a secret. All 21 are structurally incapable of starting a flow.\nThe same shape applies to go, java, cpp and rust, whose attribute counts are\nNOT broken out here and are unmeasured rather than known-small.\n\nWHY THIS IS FILED SEPARATELY FROM WI-pimun (P2, same anchoring, different\nclaim). WI-pimun says a consumer \"cannot tell which function performs the I/O\"\n-- an ATTRIBUTION gap, and its reproducer is python-specific\n(`subprocess.Popen`, a calls edge). This is the SECURITY consequence of the\nsame anchor in a different producer: an attribute source cannot participate in\ntaint propagation at all, so a real `process.env` -> `fs.writeFileSync` leak\nreturns `confirmed` rc 0. That is a false confirm, not a missing label, and it\nis not reachable from WI-pimun's description. Cross-referenced deliberately\nrather than folded: closing WI-pimun's python calls-edge case would not touch\nthis, and someone reading WI-pimun would not learn that js/ts taint is blind to\n`process.env`.\n\nFIX SHAPE (not costed, and the reason INV-potuf shipped without it). The helper\nalready accepts a per-function root, so the change is at the five CALL SITES,\nnot in the helper -- but it moves the `src` of every attribute-ref edge in five\nlanguages, which re-anchors io-boundary chains, and the double-emission\nquestion (a file-root walk descends into function bodies) has to be answered\nbefore it is safe. That is a larger blast radius than the alias fix it was\ndiscovered by, and the freeze rule is minimal independently-revertable PRs.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING for whoever takes it: this ADDS findings (attribute sources\nstart participating). That is the safe direction, but it should still be\nmeasured on both signs, and on more than javascript."  # 93a4
    fields:  # 93a4
      statement: "A taint source must be anchored to the callable that performs the read, or it cannot participate in propagation. VIOLATED for every tree-sitter analyzer (js_ts, go, java, cpp, rust): emit_module_attribute_refs is called with the FILE pseudo-symbol as caller_symbol, so a module_attr_ref edge's src is the file while the sink's src is the function, and the two never share a caller. Measured: process.env.API_KEY -> fs.writeFileSync returns confirmed rc 0, while os.hostname() -> fs.writeFileSync in the same function returns violated rc 1."  # 93a4
      root_cause: "emit_module_attribute_refs documents that its root argument may be a function body for per-function emission, but all five tree-sitter call sites pass the file root and a file pseudo-symbol (js_ts.py:5979, go.py:3186, java.py:2604, cpp.py:1689, rust.py:2580). Python is unaffected because its own WI-guhok helper anchors to the enclosing callable."  # 93a4
