- op: discuss  # 7f0e
  at: '2026-08-15T19:39:31Z'  # 7f0e
  by: agent  # 7f0e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7f0e
  clock: 3  # 7f0e
  nonce: 7f0e  # 7f0e
  message: "SATISFIED. PR #356, measured end to end rather than at the analyzer. One JS file holding both shapes in sibling functions: os.hostname() -> fs.writeFileSync was already found (a CALL, anchored to its function) while process.env.API_KEY -> fs.writeFileSync was missed (an ATTRIBUTE, anchored to the file). After: 2 flows instead of 1, and the edge reads src=javascript:app.js:4-7:leakEnv:function. All five tree-sitter call sites now pass enclosing_symbols; a parity test enumerates them so the next analyzer fails a test rather than silently repeating this. Resolved by LINE SPAN rather than by walking to a function node, so the rule needs no per-language knowledge of callable node kinds and lives once. A genuinely module-level read still anchors to the file, which is correct and asserted. The tripwire test that pinned the defect went red exactly as its docstring predicted and was replaced with the positive assertion it named, plus one asserting source and sink SHARE an anchor. Three of my own errors on the way, each caught by measuring: a scripted edit anchored on a pattern put the kwarg inside the wrong call in rust and cpp; the js_ts path index keyed on ABSOLUTE paths while the lookup used a RELATIVE name, so the fix silently did nothing and the verdict was unchanged; and Symbol.span is a Span object, not a tuple, so len() raised inside the analyzer and the pipeline swallowed it into a 0-edge analysis."  # 7f0e
